.\" Version: 1.2
.\"
.TH SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout 8 "16 Aug 2026" "" "SAPStartSrv"
.\"
.SH NAME
.\"
SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout \- Alert agent for cluster timeout alerts.
.PP
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\"
SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout can be used to react on Linux cluster RA timeout alerts.
.PP
The Linux cluster provides an interface to initiate external actions when a
cluster event occurs (alert). Than the cluster calls an external program (an
alert agent) to handle that alert.
.PP
When a Linux cluster resource agent run into an timeout, the cluster can call
SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout on each active cluster node.
.\" TODO for troubleshooting only
.br
See also manual pages SAPStartSrv-helper(8), ocf_suse_SAPStartSrv(7) and
ocf_heartbeat_SAPInstance(7).
.PP
.B SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout is a technology preview.
.PP
.\"
.SH SUPPORTED PARAMETERS
.TP
\fBtimeout\fR
If the alert agent does not complete within this amount of time, it will be terminated.
Optional, default "30s". Example "meta timeout=30s".
.TP
\fBalert_sid\fR
SAP SID of to handle. Might be used by custom helper scripts.
Optional, default "EN2". Example "attributes alert_sid=ADA".
.TP
\fBalert_ino\fR
SAP instance number of to handle. Might be used by custom helper scripts.
Optional, default "00". Example "attributes alert_ino=22". 
.TP
\fBalert_cmd\fR
Command to call. Might be used to name a custom helper script.
Optional, default "/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-helper".
Example "alert_cmd=/root/bin/dumpstack".
See manual page SAPStartSrv-helper(8).
.PP
.\"
.SH RETURN CODES
.\"
.B 0
Successful program execution.
.br
.B >0
Usage, syntax or execution errors.
.br
In addition log entries are written, which can be scanned by using a pattern
like "SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout".
.PP
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.\"
\fB*\fR Simple example configuration for the timeout alert handler.
.PP
The following lines needs to be added to the cluster´s CIB:
.PP
.RS 2
alert timeout-1 "/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Simple example for configuring the alert agent by using crm.
.PP
Alternate way for configuring the alert agent.
.PP
.RS 2
# crm configure alert timeout-1 \\
.br
 "/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Advanced example configuration for the timeout alert handler.
.PP
A custom script /root/bin/dumpstack is used, SID is EN2 instance number 00.
.\" TODO what script?
.PP
.RS 2
alert timeout-1 "/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout" \\
.br
 select resources \\
.br
 attributes alert_sid=ADA alert_ino=00 \\
.br 
 alert_cmd=/root/bin/dumpstack
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Showing all configured alert agents.
.PP
.RS 2
# crm configure show type:alert
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Showing agent messages.
.PP
.RS 2
# grep SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout /var/log/messages
.RE
.PP
\fB*\fR Example for sudo permissions in /etc/sudoers.d/SAPStartSrv .
.PP
See also manual pages sudoers(5) and SAPStartSrv-helper(8).
.PP
.RS 2
# SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout needs
.br
hacluster ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-helper *
.RE
.PP
.\"
.SH FILES
.TP
/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout
the alert agent
.TP
/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-helper
the default agent helper
.TP
/etc/sudoers.d/
directory for sudoers config files
.PP
.\"
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.\"
* SAPStartSrv-alert-timeout should be activated only, when requested by support.
.PP
* No other alert agent should be configured for the resources alert.
.PP
* User hacluster is member of group haclient. Both are defined locally on each
cluster nodes.
.PP
* User hacluster needs password-less sudo permission on "/usr/bin/SAPStartSrv-helper".
.PP
* To call sapstack, gdb is needed.
.PP
* The customer is responsible for any custom script called by the alert agent.
.PP
* The alert agent runtime almost completely depends on call-outs to OS and
Linux cluster.
.PP
